Scope of this addendum:

This BSD 2-Clause addendum covers code added or modified by the
phasm-stego branch on top of Cisco OpenH264 v2.6.0. The patches expose
CABAC bin-emit hooks, mode-decision cost capture, and supporting C ABI
surface to enable steganographic operations in the phasm.app stack.

Cisco Systems, Inc.'s original OpenH264 code remains under the
BSD 2-Clause license in the sibling LICENSE file at the repository root.
Both licenses are BSD-2-Clause and fully compatible; redistributors must
honor both copyright notices.

The H.264 / AVC patent obligations to MPEG LA / Via LA are independent
of this software license and are unaffected by either BSD-2-Clause
grant. Cisco's signed openh264.org binary distribution program does NOT
extend to derivative binaries built from this fork; downstreams that
distribute binaries assemble their own Via LA AVC compliance posture.

